00:43:48,571 --> 00:43:54,571
is a 2023 British documentary film about the English pop duo Wham!

11
00:48:11,428 --> 00:48:17,428
consisting of George Michael and Andrew Ridgeley.

12
00:52:34,285 --> 00:52:40,285
The film marks the 40th anniversary of their 1983 debut album Fantastic.

13
00:56:57,142 --> 00:57:03,142
Directed by Chris Smith it relies primarily on rare archive footage and audio interviews by the duo, including television appearances, concert footage,
private home video, behind-the-scenes outtakes, and family comments all linked together using scrapbooks created by Ridgeley's mother.

14
01:01:19,999 --> 01:01:25,999
The film was co-produced by Ventureland / Passion Pictures, Nemperor Production, and
Library Films with Altitude Film and Netflix serving as distributors.

15
01:05:42,857 --> 01:05:48,857
had its world premiere at the Sheffield DocFest on 17–18 June 2023 and given a
limited theatrical release in the United Kingdom on 27 June.

16
01:10:05,714 --> 01:10:11,714
It was reviewed as a cleverly stitched together film, using audio
posthumously of Michael and new audio from Ridgeley.

17
01:14:28,571 --> 01:14:34,571
It was released worldwide to stream on 5 July 2023 on Netflix and
received generally positive reviews from critics.

18
01:18:51,428 --> 01:18:57,428
The film was nominated for a BAFTA Award for Best Documentary.

19
01:23:14,285 --> 01:23:20,285
The film explores themes of friendship, pop culture,
archive footage, nostalgic, 1980s.

20
01:27:37,142 --> 01:27:43,142
The tone is emotional.
